WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:21.700
DesignX is an accelerator and

00:00:21.710 --> 00:00:24.200
educational program that's focused on

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:27.230
design and the built environment.

00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:29.330
The program allows students to take

00:00:29.330 --> 00:00:32.509
what they are creating here at MIT— in

00:00:32.509 --> 00:00:35.539
studios, in classes, ideas they may have

00:00:35.539 --> 00:00:38.810
developed on their own—and to use those

00:00:38.810 --> 00:00:40.790
and develop those while they're in

00:00:40.790 --> 00:00:42.500
school to launch them into their

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:45.500
professional careers or to new businesses.

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:50.300
DesignX is looking not first

00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:52.399
at the business but but really at the

00:00:52.399 --> 00:00:55.520
problem and the design solution for it.

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:58.520
Students here don't shy away from those

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:00.050
and that's what I'm really excited about:

00:01:00.050 --> 00:01:03.670
is giving them the tools to address those challenges.

00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:08.900
We sense how spaces are used.

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:11.820
The developers have the means and capacity to do this today.

00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:15.440
We're bringing these opportunities to the masses, to our members.

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:19.420
At this point we're envisioning it as a set of computer science materials.

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:23.300
Once you're in the program, there's a business workshop

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:26.680
and a full-on accelerator studio.

00:01:26.680 --> 00:01:28.840
Where they work on their ideas

00:01:28.840 --> 00:01:32.380
and turn them into marketable products or processes.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:35.000
You're receiving mentorship from

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:39.360
professionals, from business people, from industry experts.

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:41.780
The research that we do at DesignX

00:01:41.780 --> 00:01:43.400
is immediately being fed

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:45.680
back into the educational platform.

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:47.660
We're finding gaps

00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:50.840
in the existing organizational structure

00:01:50.850 --> 00:01:54.350
to identify where should our new organizations

00:01:54.350 --> 00:01:55.680
head in the direction towards.

00:01:55.860 --> 00:01:58.340
With our partners in industry this could be

00:01:58.350 --> 00:02:00.330
a chance to take an idea and actually deploy it,

00:02:00.330 --> 00:02:02.890
to test it in a real-life setting.

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:05.720
We'll have a two-way flow of information:

00:02:05.720 --> 00:02:07.860
to understand the challenges from the real world

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:09.840
and bring those into DesignX,

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:11.880
and to take the products and the solutions

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:13.300
that we're developing here

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:14.720
and push them out into the world.

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:16.040
They're transforming cities.

00:02:16.050 --> 00:02:19.170
They are developing new approaches

00:02:19.170 --> 00:02:22.830
to design and ways for people to live.

00:02:22.830 --> 00:02:26.580
This is a school that is based on creativity

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:28.360
and interaction with communities

00:02:28.420 --> 00:02:31.020
and making life better for people.

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:35.080
That's the whole mission of the school.

